{"id": "EUVD-2026-82282", "enisaUuid": "8e5818d8-8b11-3d89-8414-7222ddd1f79e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Copy per-CPU map value padding in copy_map_value_long()\n\nIn kernel, per-CPU map elements are stored with\nround_up(map->value_size, 8) bytes. On UAPI lookup paths, it copies the\nrounded size for each CPU into a temporary buffer.\n\nHowever, copy_map_value_long() passes 'map->value_size' to\nbpf_obj_memcpy(). When the map has special fields, bpf_obj_memcpy() copies\naround those fields with memcpy(), and does not copy the tail padding\nbetween 'map->value_size' and round_up(map->value_size, 8).\n\nThe temporary UAPI lookup buffers are allocated without __GFP_ZERO. As a\nresult, when the per-CPU map's value size is not equal to\nround_up(map->value_size, 8), UAPI LOOKUP_ELEM and its variants can return\nstale heap contents from that padding to user space. The same issue\napplies to bpf_iter for per-CPU maps.\n\nPass round_up(map->value_size, 8) to bpf_obj_memcpy() from\ncopy_map_value_long(), so per-CPU maps both with and without special\nfields copy the entire per-CPU slot. Remove the now redundant round_up()\nfrom bpf_obj_memcpy()'s long_memcpy path.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:12:03", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:06:45", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/953e85da53541a8dc3e7ad4e8532f29a34a32eae", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/003bf840ed3326bd01396ce7d5b431cef0d371e7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5e9f69829835521aa2942d1d14bd0990fbc6991e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ff3f22ed8d2f350b4c24ee26e33daea5f08d58ef", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7cf9cd98cf6f0df3befc167ca6b54c07014d71de"], "aliases": ["GHSA-2m7j-g554-hf69", "CVE-2026-93174"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "02779861-065d-3904-8836-761c967e98d9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "448325199f574d33824dbf9121efb03558412966 <7cf9cd98cf6f0df3befc167ca6b54c07014d71de"}, {"id": "1c4ae302-ce66-394e-8b14-35d80afb8216", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "448325199f574d33824dbf9121efb03558412966 <953e85da53541a8dc3e7ad4e8532f29a34a32eae"}, {"id": "3db1e4fe-9d68-38a4-a40b-b6e324f1218b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "448325199f574d33824dbf9121efb03558412966 <5e9f69829835521aa2942d1d14bd0990fbc6991e"}, {"id": "862d6ef7-8401-39b6-897c-4f1cfd09e22f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "86304eab-23c4-3248-a682-a87017155753", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "90ed3f80-8853-396a-8886-7c051c4d36e2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "448325199f574d33824dbf9121efb03558412966 <003bf840ed3326bd01396ce7d5b431cef0d371e7"}, {"id": "94043f60-2d4f-34a6-83df-4a23e0fca93f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "bafa2a1c-90ed-3d35-9530-e57ca40e8050", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "e34b1e92-90d3-3fe2-b047-9aaff3a332d8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "e5fd2445-5b61-3b06-8640-2940977ff113", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "448325199f574d33824dbf9121efb03558412966 <ff3f22ed8d2f350b4c24ee26e33daea5f08d58ef"}, {"id": "ebaec7fe-6751-3d10-95e3-96a2348541b6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.1"}, {"id": "ee539452-2d84-399d-9243-be6df13b6b76", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1840a798-748b-3203-9436-181220b1fb79", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited":